{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat upon the blood.</b> This verse warns against a species of sorcery that was practiced in those times: they would pour the blood into a pit, and the demons would gather there and eat around the pit, and the demons too with them; and since they ate and derived benefit from it, they would reveal the future to them. This practice was customary among the Egyptians, and Israel learned it from them — so much so that they went astray after them; therefore Scripture needed this warning. <br> And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: <b>You shall not eat upon the blood</b> — this is a warning that a person should not eat before prayer; as they said: Do not eat before you have prayed for your blood. <br>And they further interpreted it: <b>You shall not eat upon the blood</b> — a warning to judges not to render judgments in capital cases except in the morning. And for this reason the Torah commanded to fast on Yom HaKippurim, for it is the day of judgment in capital cases, so that eating not distract a person from finding his desire in the ways of repentance and forgiveness. And if in the case of another person's life he is warned by this verse, then by a fortiori he must be careful with his own life not to be negligent — for if he is negligent, it is he himself who loses his life and destroys his own soul; and it need not be said only in capital cases, but even in monetary cases it was said thus, because it is stated (Jeremiah 21): ״דינו לבקר משפט״, and they said: Do not render judgment [after eating and drinking]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The closing phrase 'אכל ושתה אל יורה' ('do not render judgment after eating and drinking') is a truncated form of the rabbinic dictum found in b. Sanhedrin 31a; rendered as printed, with the implied subject (judges) carried over from the preceding clause."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:06.089453566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}